(39, 2197, 'Following a review of the assigned Dossier, Additional information has been requested for the Administrative, Quality, and Clinical sections of the application. The queries are posted on the attached report/', 1788, '2024-11-04 11:19:03', 1),
(40, 1944, 'The applicant should answer the queries', 1874, '2024-11-04 11:23:37', 1),
(41, 2196, '1. You are requested to apply for GMP inspection of the finished immunogenic product manufacturing facility i.e Health Care Formulations Pvt Ltd., C/8, Sardar Estate, Ajwa Road, City: Vadodara – 390 019, Dist. Vadodara, Gujarat State, India. Your application should include submission of the current site master file and an application fee.\r\n2. You are requested to submit valid copy of manufacturing license and/or GMP certificate for the API manufacturing site Bal Pharma Limited, 61-B, Bommasandra Industrial Area Bangalore – 560 099, India.\r\n3. You are requested to undertake a risk assessment study to determine the presence and identify the sources of nitrosamines impurities contamination in your API.  If contamination is present appropriate limits should be put in place to ensure control of such impurities below the acceptable levels in line with the principles outlined in the ICH M7 Guideline.\r\n4. You are requested to submit specification and analytical methods for the API from the FPP manufacturer. Analytical method verification should also be submitted for compendial method while full validation report is required for non-compendial methods. Note that all tests included in the API specifications from the API manufacturer should be controlled by the FPP manufacturer. In addition, tighten the limit for control of Benzene to NMT 2 ppm.\r\n5. It was noted that data for validating the absence of Nickel were generated by SHIVA Analytical (India) Private Limited. Please clarify the relationship between SHIVA Analytical and the API manufacturer. If a formal agreement exists, submit an authorized contract specifying the responsibilities of each party.\r\n6. You are requested to submit specification and analytical method for the container closure system of the API from the API manufacturer. The documents should be submitted in a controlled official document that is signed, dated and bearing specification control and version number.\r\n7. You are requested to submit the study to demonstrate the suitability of the dosing device and its graduation as per EMA guideline EMEA/CHMP/QWP/178621/2004. In addition, the reproducibility of the measuring cup that will consistently deliver the intended volume should be demonstrated. \r\n8. Please note that the amount of antimicrobial preservative (i.e. Sodium Methyl Paraben and Sodium Propyl Paraben) used in your drug product formulation Ebastan Syrup (Ebastine Oral Solution BP 5 mg/5 ml) should be justified by the submission of results of studies on the product formulated with different concentrations of the preservatives to demonstrate the least necessary but still effective concentrations. The effectiveness of each agent should be justified and verified by appropriate studies (e.g. USP or Ph. Eur. general chapters on antimicrobial preservatives) using a batch of the FPP. Note that, the safety of the preservatives should be supported by bibliographic and /or experimental data.  \r\n9. With respect to the manufacturing process of the FPP, please provide a full detailed executed batch manufacturing records for at least one batch of FPP. Also, provide master production documents (MPD/blank BMR) for the proposed commercial production batch size(s) that includes the following: \r\ni.	Provide a detailed narrative description and flow diagram of the manufacturing process to include the make/model, capacity and equipment number of all key production equipments, a tabulated list of equipment may be included. \r\nii.	Include the formula for adjustment of batch quantities of the API to be dispensed based on potency of API and LOD/water content as a footnote to the table;\r\niii.	Include the sampling plan for every critical stage as documented in the process validation protocol (steps, number of samples and frequency of testing) \r\niv.	During bulk mixing, the in-process control test for appearance pH, weight per ml, specific gravity and assay should be included.\r\nv.	During filling, the in-process control test for appearance, assay, fill volume, microbial limits and leak test should be included. \r\nvi.	The maximum holding time for the intermediate (bulk solution) prior to filling should be specified in the dossier and production documents. Individual holding time and cumulative holding time above 30 days and 90 days respectively should be supported by stability data.; and\r\nYour response should include the submission of the revised in-process specifications for each critical stage included with reference/version number, signed and dated by responsible personnel, and master production records/blank BMR with a complete list of changes, or a statement that no unsolicited changes have been made should be submitted. The QIS in respective section 2.3.P.3.3 and 2.3.P.3.4 should also be updated accordingly.\r\n\r\n', 1789, '2024-11-08 11:59:33', 1),
(44, 2531, 'Vitafer forte is declared to be for Therapeutic use, Upon careful review, we have identified the need for additional information to complete your application process. To facilitate this, we kindly request you to submit complete module 1,2,3,4 and module 5 in pdf format together with Quality Overall Summary (QOS) and Quality Information Summary (QIS) in MS words on email: hmdar@rwandafda.gov.rw and related samples at Rwanda FDA reception along with there certificate of analysis. Please note that you will not be requested to pay additional registration fees, the existing proof of payment will be sent along with the previous application letter for confirmation. \r\n\r\nKindly resubmit your application not later than 90 days from the date of receipt of this letter. After the provided timeline, we will consider your application as withdrawn. Please refer to Regulation Governing Registration of Medicinal Products, especially in article 12.', 1802, '2024-11-11 11:11:07', 1),
(45, 1420, 'Additional information requested', 1778, '2024-11-14 12:18:11', 1),
(46, 2552, 'The provided Patient Information Leaflet (PIL) is not in the recommended format. Since the PIL is mandatory for being published on Rwanda FDA website, please ensure compliance with our regulatory requirements and provide the product information in line with Guidance on format and content of the PIL available on Rwanda FDA website.\r\nSee link below:\r\nhttps://rwandafda.gov.rw/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Guidance-on-Format-and-Content-of-Patient-Information-Leaflets-for-human-medicinal-Products.pdf.\r\nThe PIL content should be clear for patient’ easy guidance and understanding and must therefore include the information such as:\r\na.	What (product name) is and what it is used for,\r\nb.	Before you <take><use> (product name)\r\nc.	How to<take>><use> (product name)\r\nd.	Possible side effects\r\ne.	How to store (product name)\r\nf.	Further information\r\nThe PIL will be published on Rwanda FDA website and the information should be in line with the set requirements in the above-mentioned guidelines, and the content should be clear for patient’ easy guidance and understanding.\r\nWe appreciate your cooperation in fulfilling this requirement and look forward to receiving the requested product information from you within the next twenty-four (24) months from the date of certificate issuance. \r\nPlease note that failure to submit the requested product information within the specified timeframe may result in the suspension of the certificate.', 1903, '2024-12-03 11:18:55', 1),
(47, 19488, 'Additional data Requested', 1908, '2025-04-01 05:01:55', 1);
